WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.356 --> 00:00:15.542
This was a giant!

2
00:00:16.202 --> 00:00:18.683
His shiny, bald head touched the ceiling.

3
00:00:20.004 --> 00:00:23.005
A curly, black beard covered half his face.

4
00:00:24.526 --> 00:00:28.608
Muscles bulged on his brown arms, chest, and shoulders.

5
00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:33.917
The genie wore black silk pants and big gold earrings.

6
00:00:33.937 --> 00:00:36.518
"Who is this?"

7
00:00:37.218 --> 00:00:38.038
cried Zeba.

8
00:00:38.058 --> 00:00:40.179
"Where did he come from?"

9
00:00:40.199 --> 00:00:42.239
"He's a genie!"

10
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.200
answered Aladdin, leaping to his mother's side.

11
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.421
"He came from the lamp."

12
00:00:48.761 --> 00:00:50.042
"Send him away!"

13
00:00:50.542 --> 00:00:51.322
begged Zeba.

14
00:00:51.342 --> 00:00:52.802
"I'm afraid."

15
00:00:52.822 --> 00:00:58.224
"I am the genie of the wonderful lamp!"

16
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.262
said the genie, crossing his arms over his huge, bare chest.

17
00:01:03.282 --> 00:01:06.203
"Do not send me away.

18
00:01:06.223 --> 00:01:09.865
I am your slave, ready to serve you."

19
00:01:11.045 --> 00:01:14.987
"I don't want a slave," Zeba said, shaking with fear.

20
00:01:16.387 --> 00:01:17.568
She turned to her son.

21
00:01:17.588 --> 00:01:19.589
"Tell him to leave, please."

22
00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:24.451
Aladdin snatched the lamp from his mother's hand.

23
00:01:25.631 --> 00:01:28.933
"Do not listen to my mother, genie of the lamp," ordered Aladdin.

24
00:01:28.953 --> 00:01:31.315
"My mother and I are hungry!

25
00:01:31.855 --> 00:01:33.576
Bring us food a sultan would eat!"

26
00:01:35.237 --> 00:01:36.698
The genie disappeared!

27
00:01:37.859 --> 00:01:41.602
But before Aladdin could even blink his eyes, the genie was back.

28
00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:47.446
He carried a large silver tray with six gold plates of food on it.

29
00:01:48.727 --> 00:01:51.009
He put the plates on a carpet on the floor.

30
00:01:51.029 --> 00:01:53.211
"What a feast!"

31
00:01:53.791 --> 00:01:54.752
Aladdin shouted.

32
00:01:56.664 --> 00:01:59.246
There was sausage made from beef and lamb.

33
00:02:00.327 --> 00:02:03.829
There was a dish piled high with beet salad and turnips.

34
00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:12.595
Other plates held rice and beans, olives, nuts, and cheese tarts—which smelled so good!

35
00:02:14.156 --> 00:02:17.459
Then—poof—the genie was gone!

36
00:02:17.479 --> 00:02:19.740
"Mother, come!"

37
00:02:20.141 --> 00:02:21.381
cried Aladdin with joy.

38
00:02:21.401 --> 00:02:24.684
"Let's enjoy this feast that has been given to us."

39
00:02:26.932 --> 00:02:28.793
"No!" answered Zeba.

40
00:02:28.813 --> 00:02:30.634
"I will not eat it.

41
00:02:31.494 --> 00:02:33.595
That terrible genie frightens me!"

42
00:02:33.615 --> 00:02:39.337
"Sit down here with me," he laughed, patting the carpet next to him.

43
00:02:39.357 --> 00:02:41.058
"Eat and be glad!"

44
00:02:42.819 --> 00:02:47.620
At last, Zeba gave in, sat down, and picked up a cheese tart.

45
00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:52.042
She had never tasted anything like it.

46
00:02:53.323 --> 00:02:56.284
It truly was food for a sultan's table.

47
00:02:59.296 --> 00:03:03.198
"Tell me, son," said Zeba, pouring Aladdin a cup of coffee.

48
00:03:03.218 --> 00:03:07.501
"Was this the genie who freed you from the enchanted treasury?"

49
00:03:09.202 --> 00:03:11.103
"No, no," answered Aladdin.

50
00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:13.725
"The genie of the ring freed me.

51
00:03:14.785 --> 00:03:17.167
He was funny-looking, Mother, and not very tall.

52
00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:19.948
He had bells hanging from his cap."

53
00:03:21.029 --> 00:03:24.731
Aladdin remembered the little, apricot-colored genie and laughed.

54
00:03:26.592 --> 00:03:29.974
"The genie of the lamp is a different kind of genie, I think," he added.

55
00:03:29.994 --> 00:03:33.957
"Yes!" said Aladdin's mother.

56
00:03:33.977 --> 00:03:36.799
"He tried to scare me to death!"

57
00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:46.005
She leaned toward Aladdin and spoke in a whisper, "Son, you must throw the lamp away—and the ring

58
00:03:46.065 --> 00:03:46.405
as well.

59
00:03:47.566 --> 00:03:49.347
They will bring us only trouble!"

60
00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:53.670
"I will not, Mother," said Aladdin.

61
00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:56.412
"We must accept our good fortune.

62
00:03:57.484 --> 00:04:01.046
Think about it—Magrib traveled all this way looking for this lamp.

63
00:04:02.386 --> 00:04:05.247
He wanted only this one thing from the enchanted treasury.

64
00:04:06.248 --> 00:04:08.929
It must be very important, so we will keep the lamp."

65
00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:11.590
"And the ring?"

66
00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:12.930
said Zeba.

67
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.232
"The ring too," said Aladdin.

68
00:04:16.252 --> 00:04:20.133
"Without the ring, I would still be buried alive.

69
00:04:21.714 --> 00:04:23.495
You would never have seen me again.

70
00:04:23.515 --> 00:04:26.676
I will never take this ring off my finger."

71
00:04:28.464 --> 00:04:30.688
Aladdin's mother sighed and shook her head.

72
00:04:30.708 --> 00:04:33.893
"Do what you want," she said.

73
00:04:33.913 --> 00:04:37.859
"But I don't want to see that horrible genie again!"
